# Submission recovery follow-up

- Give refused local retirement of a write-mode switch its own withdrawal
  failure fact. Today driver.withdrawControl retains the switch and publishes a
  new unsaved occurrence, but the row says "Couldn't switch" with Retry (Stop
  remains available). If storage refuses deletion, recovery should retry the
  withdrawal rather than post the switch. Predates F3a; accepted P3 in the F3a
  structural/alignment sign-offs. Map the owner's fact to switch-withdraw-failed.
